						Security Alert: U.S. Embassy Addis Ababa, Ethiopia (October 15, 2026) 
					</div>

						
				</div>

			</div>

		</section>

<section  class="ga-content-block stacking-slide white-section-background-color paragraphsection">
	<div class="paragraph alignwide container meta-info-top">

		
	</div>

	<div class="paragraph alignwide container">

		<div class="row">

			
				<p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Ethiopia</p>
<p><strong>Event: </strong> The U.S. Embassy continues to monitor events in northern Ethiopia. Ethiopian National Defense Forces and Tigray Peace Forces have made further territorial gains and civil administration is being established in the Tigray region. Recent fighting has greatly subsided in the Tigray, Amhara, and Afar Regions.</p>
<p>Ethiopian Airlines resumed flights to and from Mekelle’s Alula Aba Nega Airport on October 11. Flights remain suspended at the airports in Axum and Shire. The Embassy does not know when flights at those airports will resume. Contact the airline directly to book tickets and for notifications on operations.</p>
<p>U.S. citizens are reminded to reconsider travel to Ethiopia. U.S. citizens are advised not to travel to the Amhara Region (including Lalibela), the Tigray Region, or the Afar Region for any reason. U.S. citizens in those areas should leave if it is safe to do so or shelter in place until conditions improve.</p>
<p>Some social media accounts contain false and intentionally misleading reports about the security situation in Ethiopia. U.S. citizens are urged to verify information using multiple sources of reliable information. Review the State Department <a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Ftravel.state.gov%252Fen%252Finternational-travel%252Ftravel-advisories%252Fethiopia.html%2F1%2F010101a14140981d-5753cb82-0f1d-4a2d-a812-4a2e88d4c1c6-000000%2F9UUU6bIqpA2EOFsJE6_qMxhPedkAslQS0mMuACsevfQ%3D452&amp;data=05%7C02%7CMesfinD%40state.gov%7Cc03369aca6494b8c055b08df2b3ff729%7C66cf50745afe48d1a691a12b2121f44b%7C0%7C0%7C639277225923948823%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=nZbDPYR%2BdYrgAy54%2BEYmz%2Bk%2B36%2BOAJKxwsjtDRlSDPQ%3D&amp;reserved=0">Travel Advisory</a> for Ethiopia and enroll in <a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fmytravel.state.gov%252Fs%252Fstep%2F1%2F010101a14140981d-5753cb82-0f1d-4a2d-a812-4a2e88d4c1c6-000000%2FjM-pnZJ_p8h2SWuchv2wG4hlj361VNhXGm_a7tBZa7s%3D452&amp;data=05%7C02%7CMesfinD%40state.gov%7Cc03369aca6494b8c055b08df2b3ff729%7C66cf50745afe48d1a691a12b2121f44b%7C0%7C0%7C639277225923976220%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=W%2FICgEx3Wj%2BZvOLJ%2BkObnNRpmxVsVijgI5K0onVt1Xg%3D&amp;reserved=0">Smart Traveler Enrollment Program (STEP)</a> for more information.</p>
<p><strong>Actions to take:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Avoid Ethiopian military installations.</li>
<li>Do not travel to Amhara (including Lalibela), Tigray, or Afar.</li>
<li>Monitor multiple, reliable local news sources for security updates.</li>
<li>Review your personal security plans.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Assistance:</strong></p>
<p>U.S. Embassy <a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fet.usembassy.gov%252F%2F1%2F010101a14140981d-5753cb82-0f1d-4a2d-a812-4a2e88d4c1c6-000000%2FK02KLIoM9cD1kTo9GQrZpPo-Vr4m06JpnBdlnLKscJ4%3D452&amp;data=05%7C02%7CMesfinD%40state.gov%7Cc03369aca6494b8c055b08df2b3ff729%7C66cf50745afe48d1a691a12b2121f44b%7C0%7C0%7C639277225923996061%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=vjNFMzkXmOBYT2jwaRyeWirgO5RR96yqfaBVwGFm4eU%3D&amp;reserved=0">Ethiopia</a></p>
