	<div class="paragraph alignwide container">

		<div class="row">

			
				<p><p><strong data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Security Alert: U.S. Embassy Addis Ababa, Ethiopia (September 25, 2026)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Location: </strong>Addis Ababa, Ethiopia</p>
<p><strong>Event: </strong>Crowds and traffic anticipated for the Meskel holiday</p>
<p>In preparation for the Meskel holiday, the police presence will increase throughout Addis Ababa and most major cities, along with checkpoints and vehicle searches. Security checkpoints will be established on many roads and at major gathering points, especially at night.</p>
<p>Beginning on September 26, in Addis Ababa, expect:</p>
<ul>
<li>Road closures, heavy traffic, and pedestrian congestion at major intersections and Orthodox churches.</li>
<li>All roads leading to and around Meskel Square to be congested or closed (see below).</li>
</ul>
<p>The following routes are typically closed for this event:</p>
<ul>
<li>Meskel Square – Bambis – Urael Church</li>
<li>Meskel Square – Filamingo – Getu Commercial – Wollo Sefer– Bole Road</li>
<li>Meskel Square – Legehar – Mexico Square</li>
<li>Meskel Square – Harambe Hotel – ENDF Ground Force HQ – Senga Tera</li>
<li>Meskel Square – ECA – National Palace – Sheraton intersection</li>
<li>Meskel Square – St. Joseph School – Meskel flower intersection (Debrezeit Road)</li>
</ul>
<p>Please follow police road closure announcements to the public as the holiday approaches. If you plan any travel in Addis Ababa, the use of alternate routes is encouraged, and otherwise expect extended traffic delays.</p>
<p><strong>Actions to take</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Monitor local media for updates</li>
<li>Avoid large crowds and gatherings</li>
<li>If caught in a large crowd, attempt to disengage</li>
<li>Be aware of your surroundings</li>
<li>Review your personal security plans</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Assistance:</strong></p>
<p>U.S. Embassy <a title="Original URL: https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fet.usembassy.gov%2F/1/010101a0d79321d6-698c7d55-fdec-459b-af81-3ed83e2fd0e3-000000/yO2CXOXL0YcANZt268Ny3EKwuE1BcPUXIQ9loVvNAzw=452. Click or tap if you trust this link." href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fet.usembassy.gov%252F%2F1%2F010101a0d79321d6-698c7d55-fdec-459b-af81-3ed83e2fd0e3-000000%2FyO2CXOXL0YcANZt268Ny3EKwuE1BcPUXIQ9loVvNAzw%3D452&amp;data=05%7C02%7CBihonBA%40state.gov%7Cb69407f42e104520156108df1adba062%7C66cf50745afe48d1a691a12b2121f44b%7C0%7C0%7C639259202726053116%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=umhuVMX9URDMPrNsCO%2BbcGHtd0HE%2FLaUfVJ3E%2BO7%2F6Y%3D&amp;reserved=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="1"><u>Ethiopia</u></a></p>
